    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 583\n\nTO THE SENATE:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nSenate Bill Number 5684-A, entitled:\n\n    \"AN ACT to amend the administrative code of the city of New York, in\n      relation to New York city transit omnibus safety requirements\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This bill would require that all New York City Transit (NYCT) buses be\nequipped,  within  five  years,  with  an L-shaped transparent partition\nconstructed with plexiglass at least one inch in thickness or some other\nsubstance of equal or greater strength. The bill would also require that\nall NYCT buses be equipped, within two years, with  a  silent  emergency\nalarm  that not only alerts the Bus Command Center of an emergency situ-\nation but also transmits the bus's location using a  Global  Positioning\nSystem (GPS) device.\n\n  This  bill's well-intentioned provisions are unnecessary in light of a\ncollective bargaining agreement that was overwhelmingly ratified on  May\n19,  2014.  Bus  operator partitions are now being installed on NYCT and\nMetropolitan Transportation Authority (MTA) Bus Company buses.   Instal-\nlation  of  these partitions should be completed by January 2017, a full\ntwo years ahead of the schedule required under this bill.  The  MTA  has\nalso agreed pursuant to a Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) to share its\nimplementation  schedule  with  and  to  keep the union representing bus\noperators updated of its progress on  retrofitting  its  bus  fleet.  In\naddition, the MTA has agreed to survey the current alarm systems on NYCT\nand  MTA buses which already transmit the exact GPS location of a bus to\nthe Bus Command Center when the covert alarm is engaged.\n\n  Furthermore, the \"one size fits all\" partition requirement in the bill\nfails to reflect the structural differences in the various bus models in\nthe existing fleet and future bus models that may  be  acquired  by  the\nMTA.  Finally, this bill is drafted to immediately prohibit the acquisi-\ntion and operation of any bus that does not have the required equipment.\nThis prohibition ignores the fact that there may be unforeseen emergency\ncircumstances that justify the use  of  an  unequipped  bus  to  provide\nrelief  and service to users in dire need. For these reasons, I am veto-\ning this bill.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 583,
